{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3060","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3060","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3060\",\"parent_revision\":\"173953dd111f61946c326ed5520916f92a26f023\",\"root_revision\":\"13acbe51317903b175f86c4359bb9e4ebe2a3aeda819ffd6d3f1a5f01d1b5f8a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe runtime strings that tell an agent what to call next steer it away from paginated navigation. The compact response's hint recommends loading full content as its first suggestion. The over-budget response tells a caller to request sections individually \u2014 advice a caller who already narrowed to one oversized section has exhausted. Neither mentions the paginated navigation parameters.\\n\\nAgents follow these strings. Documentation is a weaker lever: these are read on every call, at the moment of the decision.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:11:07.292876Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: runtime hints steer agents away from paginated navigation\\nDate: 2026-08-20\\nGoal: Make _build_compact_manifest()'s _hint and _build_over_budget_view()'s _usage in backlog_core/server.py comply with R7 (Hints must be actionable) in agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md.\\nConditions:\\n1. Exact current text/location of the two violating hint strings | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. R7 requirement text and its three prohibitions | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Existing in-package pattern for a paginated-navigation hint (disclosure_handler.py next_call) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Whether the over-budget call site has access to \\\"caller already narrowed to one section\\\" signal | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Whether disclosure_handler.py itself needs changes vs. server.py only | Status: DERIVABLE (confirm during Impact Radius)\\n6. Existing test conventions for backlog_core/server.py hint-construction functions | Status: DERIVABLE (confirm during Impact Radius / Files)\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:13:57.868084Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n\\n**Rationale**: Code in two functions violates R7 (normative requirement in agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md) by generating hints that recommend actions agents have already exhausted or actions the response cannot support.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: Direct source verification against normative requirement R7. Compared violating code against correct reference implementation in disclosure_handler.py and container-level requirement text.\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: backlog_view(summary=True) and over-budget backlog_view() responses \u2192 agent receives hint recommending full-content retrieval as first action (summary=False) or pagination actions (navigate=, skip_tokens=) not demonstrated in the response object itself.\\n\\n**Evidence Chain**:\\n- Violating location 1: server.py:2306-2309 (_build_compact_manifest._hint) recommends \\\"Load full content: summary=False\\\" first, violating R7 clause \\\"never recommend retrieving everything as its first suggestion\\\"\\n- Violating location 2: server.py:2379-2387 (_build_over_budget_view._usage) recommends \\\"request them individually\\\" without naming pagination parameters (navigate=, head=, skip_tokens=) that exist in the response sections_index but are absent from the hint itself, violating R7 clause \\\"never name a mechanism absent from the response it accompanies\\\"\\n- Correct pattern reference: disclosure_handler.py:487-490 (next_call hint) demonstrates the required form \u2014 hint uses navigate= and skip_tokens= parameters documented in the same node's bounded content structure\\n- Requirement source: agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md:159-164, R7 normative requirement\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] No hint recommends retrieving everything as its first suggestion, per R7\\n- [ ] The over-budget hint offers an action a narrowed caller has not already taken\\n- [ ] Hints name only mechanisms present in the response they accompany\\n- [ ] Addresses appearing in a hint are valid in that same response\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1 \u2014 small change, disproportionate effect on agent behaviour\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e9a41883b712060ffa69a95d910f547ab89fe19af6ae562230c9fcb3df839bb7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPx2jVg\"}"}